spans.s:
lohitaka, m.
(1) some sort of insect: ˚kā prāṇakā kālaśīrṣakā (bodhisattvasya) pādatalehi yāvaj jānumāṇḍalāni chādayitvā asthānsuḥ Mv 〔ii.137.4〕; repeated 〔138.19〕 with ˚ka-prāṇakā;
(2) n. of a town: Mv 〔iii.328.2〕; also Lohitavastuka, 〔327.20〕, and Rohitavastu, q.v.; see also Kamaṇḍaluka;
(3) n. of two nāga kings: Māy 〔247.14〕; cf. Skt. Lohita, BR s.v., 2 k. See also lohitakopadhāna.
